## Standing rules for every task

- **Migration rule (SPEC Â§9, Â§10):** a migration is done when it is written, applied to the LOCAL database, its 
integration tests pass, and its rollback SQL is recorded in the migration header and TRACK. Each gets a row in 
`spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/MIGRATIONS-PENDENTES.md`. Nothing is applied online before T15.
- **Function privilege rule (review P1):** the baseline default privileges grant EXECUTE on every new `public` 
function to `anon`, `authenticated`, and `service_role` (`20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:2131-2134`). Every 
new function therefore: has owner `postgres`, `SET search_path = ''` with schema-qualified references, `REVOKE ALL ... 
FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated, service_role`, and then an explicit `GRANT EXECUTE` only to the role that needs it; 
integration tests read the effective EXECUTE matrix from the catalog. User-facing RPCs that authorize the caller 
themselves (resolving `auth.uid()` â†’ `users.supabase_uid`) are granted to `authenticated` only. Server-only RPCs 
(key read, admission/reservation, settlement, usage maintenance) are granted to `service_role` only and are called by 
server code only after the route has authorized the application user; service role never replaces that authorization. 
Integration tests call each server-only RPC directly as `anon` and `authenticated` and expect denial.
- **Online method (T15 only):** the Phase 4/5 method â€” re-check `npx supabase migration list --linked` and the 
target catalog immediately before; apply each reviewed file's SQL transactionally and record only its version; read 
back catalog objects; smoke-check. Never `supabase db push`, `migration up --linked`, or broad `migration repair`.
- **Supabase/RLS review gate (AGENTS.md):** every migration, RLS policy, grant, RPC, repository, and API route change 
passes the `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit (users.id vs supabase_uid, server client + `auth.getUser()`, service role 
never replacing authorization, function grants per the rule above) before its task is recorded done.
- **Adversarial review gate (AGENTS.md):** direct Codex CLI, `gpt-6.1-sol`, effort `max`, read-only, per 
`delegation-anthropic.md`; prompts and results under `reviews/`. Per block, after its last task, over the block's 
combined diff: **Block A** = T1, T17, T2, T3, T4; **Block B** = T5, T6, T7, T8; **Block C** = T9, T10, T16, T11; 
**Block D** = T12, T13; **Final** = T14 over the whole work-item diff. Another round only for a High/Medium a real 
user or realistic failure can trigger; at most one fix round per block; leftovers recorded in TRACK and carried to T14.
- **Verification cadence (AGENTS.md, owner decisions 2026-10-10):** per task type-check + lint (new E2E specs are 
written with their task, not run); per block, after its fix round, type-check, lint, and the DB integration suite when 
server code changed; no E2E before T14; T14 runs every new spec and the full regression E2E once in Chrome only, zero 
retries, a failing test analysed and rerun alone. One test process at a time; nothing heavy in parallel.
- **Test policy (SPEC Â§15):** integration tests in a new `__tests__/meeting-notes-db/` suite (Vitest, node env, local 
Supabase, route handlers invoked in-process â€” same pattern as `vitest.messaging-db.config.mts`) and Playwright E2E 
with two accounts. The external AI provider is the only thing replaced, by the local fake AI server built in T16, 
reached over real HTTP. No unit tests; a touched unit test (e.g. `__tests__/company-settings-default-space.test.tsx`, 
`__tests__/modern-space-card.test.tsx`) is replaced by integration/E2E coverage and deleted, recorded in TRACK.
- **Secrets:** API keys, the ticket secret, and transcript text never in logs, errors, TRACK, reviews, or reports; 
tests use canary keys only.

