45: ## T17 — Note mutation RPCs with revision and version history
46: Reasoning: Writes must be authorized on the pre-change state and versioned atomically, at the database and not 
only at the API (BR-003/004, BR-011).
47: Task: `authenticated`-granted SECURITY DEFINER RPCs (per the function privilege rule) that resolve the caller by 
`supabase_uid`, authorize on the pre-change state, require the current revision, and in one transaction apply the 
change, bump the revision, and insert one version: create (any member, any company space incl. private, title 1–200, 
date required, participants current members only), update (fields + participants; former members already present may 
be retained; a non-editor cannot add themselves), restore (version fields incl. participants; items/transcript 
untouched; editors only), delete (author while a member, or admin; removes versions, participants, items, transcript). 
Cross-company admins are denied.
48: Done when: Every note write path through the database enforces rights, revision, limits, and versioning.
49: Verify by: Integration tests for AC-002 (DB-level limits), AC-004 (direct-client edit/self-add/restore denial for 
non-participant; cross-company admin denied), AC-005 (competing transactions incl. restore vs save), AC-006 (three 
saves → three immutable versions; non-editor restore denied; restore creates a fourth version equal to version 1 with 
items/transcript unchanged), AC-007, AC-021 (a save that keeps a former member listed succeeds; the former 
participant's edit is denied; after rejoining the same company their edit succeeds); `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit.
50: Covers: FR-001, FR-006, FR-007, FR-008, FR-009, FR-010, FR-030, BR-002, BR-003, BR-004, BR-011, AC-002, AC-004, 
AC-005, AC-006, AC-007, AC-021
51: Root: T17
