54: ## T2 — Action-item contract in the database
55: Reasoning: Items have their own rights (assignee completion only), date-only due dates, and a capacity that must 
hold under concurrency; observed `due_date timestamptz` and unrestricted schema.
56: Task: Local migrations make items carry a date-only due date, assignee id + name snapshot, description 1–1,000 
chars, a per-item revision, and immutable note/creator/creation fields. `authenticated`-granted RPCs (per the function 
privilege rule): editors create/edit/delete (assignee must be a current company member); editors and the current 
assignee toggle completion through a completion-only path; every change requires the item's current revision; capacity 
100 per note is enforced atomically for every insertion path under the note row lock (lock order rule), which T12's 
Apply also takes.
57: Done when: The local database enforces the item rules, including concurrent capacity.
58: Verify by: Integration tests for AC-008, AC-009 (below-capacity validators, capacity, date stored and returned as 
the same calendar date), AC-021 (an assignee who left cannot toggle completion; after rejoining they can), AC-032 
(99-item concurrent adds); `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit.
59: Covers: FR-011, FR-030, BR-005, AC-008, AC-009, AC-021, AC-032
